## In-Progress Cable (Drawing State)

When the user clicks an outlet to start drawing a cable:

1. Enable `pointer-events: all` on the SVG layer (so it captures mouse events)
2. Create a ghost `<path>` that follows the mouse:
   ```javascript
   canvas.addEventListener('mousemove', (e) => {
     if (!drawingState.active) return;
     const canvasRect = canvas.getBoundingClientRect();
     const mouseX = e.clientX - canvasRect.left;
     const mouseY = e.clientY - canvasRect.top;
     ghostPath.setAttribute('d', 
       `M ${drawingState.srcX} ${drawingState.srcY} L ${mouseX} ${mouseY}`
     );
   });
   ```
3. Highlight valid inlets (add CSS class `pn-inlet--valid`) as mouse approaches
4. On inlet click: create edge in PatchGraph, remove ghost path, disable SVG pointer-events
5. On Escape / click elsewhere: cancel, remove ghost path

