### 3. Message Receipt

When a message arrives at an object's inlet:

```typescript
interface PatchObjectInstance {
  id: string;
  type: string;

  // Called by the message dispatcher when a message arrives
  receiveMessage(inlet: number, msg: PatchMessage): void;
}

type PatchMessage = 
  | { type: 'bang' }
  | { type: 'float'; value: number }
  | { type: 'symbol'; value: string }
  | { type: 'list'; values: (number | string)[] };
```

The object handles the message (updating internal state, triggering audio, etc.) and may call the graph dispatcher to fire its outlets.

### 4. Outlet Fire

When an object has output to send:

```typescript
// Called by object instances to propagate output
function fireOutlet(graph: PatchGraph, nodeId: string, outlet: number, msg: PatchMessage) {
  const edges = graph.getEdgesFromOutlet(nodeId, outlet);
  for (const edge of edges) {
    const destNode = graph.nodes.get(edge.toNodeId);
    if (destNode) {
      destNode.instance.receiveMessage(edge.toInlet, msg);
    }
  }
}
```

This is synchronous and depth-first. See [[concepts/message-passing]].

