### Op Definition (simplified)
```javascript
const op = CABLES.patch.addOp("Ops.Math.Sum", {
  name: "Sum"
});
const inA = op.inFloat("A", 0);
const inB = op.inFloat("B", 0);
const outResult = op.outFloat("Result");

op.setPortGroup("Inputs", [inA, inB]);

function update() {
  outResult.set(inA.get() + inB.get());
}

inA.onChange = update;
inB.onChange = update;
```

The `onChange` callback model is essentially a **push-based reactive system** — when an input value changes, the op recomputes and pushes the result to its output port, which triggers `onChange` on any connected ports downstream.

This is conceptually close to PD's model for value/message propagation.

